    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d896">

                <pb facs="1406" n="1392" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1392"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 EW/11–2444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Representative on the United Nations War
                        Crimes Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Pell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-24">November 24,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received December 6.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that at the
                    meeting of Committee No. II, of the War Crimes Commission, held yesterday,
                    Thursday November 23, Sir Cecil Hurst, the Chairman of the Commission and
                    Commissioner for the United Kingdom, said that the British Government had taken
                    the initiative to give a directive to the Military High Command, instructing
                    them to receive our list of war criminals.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert Pell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
